# The whole shell on demo data in one take: 25 scenes, about four minutes.
# README.md, "Recording a tour". Recorded from the starting state
#   desk-nest up --demo --fixtures weather=demo-fine-day --fixtures office=demo-lights-on \
#     --fixtures fleet=demo-before --fixtures tokens=demo-week --fixtures limits=demo-week \
#     --fixtures tailscale=demo-tailnet --fixtures calendar=demo-week --fixtures cheatsheet=demo-binds
#   desk-nest record hosts/BrightFalls/users/matteo/hyprland/nest/tour/tour.steps <outdir>
# The captions are the caption steps below; captions.md holds the same text
# by scene, and the desk-nest check keeps the two the same.
# Times are seconds from the recording's start; each scene starts where the
# one before it ends. The tray click (1034, 22) is where the tray icon sits
# on DP-1 once the bar shows the snow and the heater, as it does by then.
pad 0 0

at 0.3    scene bar
at 0.7    caption 3.5 A showcase of my custom Quickshell setup on Hyprland
at 4.4    caption 3.5 The bar: workspaces, the clock with the next event, and one item per panel

at 8.3    scene launcher
at 8.6    ipc launcher toggle
at 8.7    caption 6.2 The launcher: type to filter, Enter to start
at 10.8   type mus
at 13.8   keys Escape

at 15.3   scene notifications
at 15.6   fixture notifications demo-morning
at 15.7   caption 7.2 Notifications stack at the top right, and clear with one key
at 21.8   ipc notifications dismissAll

at 23.3   scene calendar
at 23.6   ipc calendar toggle
at 23.7   caption 6.7 Under the clock: the month and today's events
at 29.8   ipc calendar toggle

at 30.8   scene calendar-full
at 31.1   ipc calendarfull toggle
at 31.2   caption 7.7 top The big view: the whole month, every event
at 37.8   ipc calendarfull toggle

at 39.3   scene weather-fine
at 39.6   ipc weather toggle
at 39.7   caption 5.2 Weather: now, the next hours, six days, air quality and an outdoor sensor (Zigbee2MQTT)

at 45.3   scene weather-rain
at 45.3   fixture weather demo-rain
at 45.7   caption 5.2 Rain, with the Met Office warning in force

at 51.3   scene weather-radar
at 51.3   keys m
at 51.7   caption 9.2 Rain radar: the past two hours, played back
at 52.8   keys space
at 60.3   keys m

at 61.3   scene weather-snow
at 61.3   fixture weather demo-snow
at 61.7   caption 6.2 And snow
at 66.8   ipc weather toggle

at 68.3   scene office
at 68.6   caption 4.4 Office: the light, the blind and the power on each socket, from Zigbee2MQTT
at 68.6   ipc office toggle
at 73.3   fixture office demo-blind-half
at 73.6   caption 3.4 The blind half down, the light dimmed
at 77.3   fixture office demo-heater
at 77.6   caption 5.9 A heater switches on: 1.5 kW, at the top of the list
at 82.3   ipc office toggle

at 83.8   scene fleet
at 84.1   caption 5.9 Fleet: NixOS and macOS machines, deployed from one repository by comin
at 84.1   ipc fleet toggle
at 90.3   fixture fleet demo-deploying
at 90.6   caption 4.4 This computer switches by hand; the others follow by themselves
at 95.3   fixture fleet demo-after
at 95.6   caption 6.4 All on the new commit; one waits for a reboot
at 100.8  ipc fleet toggle

at 102.3  scene tailscale
at 102.6  ipc tailscale toggle
at 102.7  caption 7.7 Tailscale: every device in the tailnet, direct or relayed
at 109.3  ipc tailscale toggle

at 110.8  scene tokens
at 111.1  caption 4.9 Claude usage: plan limits, today, and the last 30 days
at 111.1  ipc tokens toggle
at 116.3  keys p
at 116.6  caption 3.4 By project
at 120.3  keys d
at 120.6  caption 3.4 Day by day
at 124.3  keys Escape
at 125.3  ipc tokens toggle

at 126.8  scene system-idle
at 126.8  fixture system demo-idle
at 127.1  ipc system toggle
at 127.2  caption 5.7 System: CPU, memory, both GPUs and storage, at rest

at 133.3  scene system-busy
at 133.3  fixture system demo-busy
at 133.7  caption 6.2 Under load: a game on the card, a build on the CPU

at 140.3  scene system-hot
at 140.3  fixture system demo-hot
at 140.7  caption 8.2 Near the limits: the readings turn orange
at 147.3  ipc system toggle
at 147.8  fixture system demo-idle

at 149.3  scene audio
at 149.6  ipc audio toggle
at 149.7  caption 7.2 Audio: the DAC's format, what is playing, and live levels
at 156.3  ipc audio toggle

at 157.3  scene volume
at 157.6  fixture audio demo-volume-up
at 157.7  caption 7.7 Volume keys show a small overlay
at 158.6  fixture audio demo-volume-up
at 159.9  fixture audio demo-volume-down
at 161.3  fixture audio demo-mute
at 163.3  fixture audio demo-mute

at 165.8  scene bluetooth
at 166.1  caption 3.9 Bluetooth: paired devices, with their batteries
at 166.1  ipc bluetooth toggle
at 170.3  fixture bluetooth demo-all
at 170.6  caption 3.4 A mouse connects
at 174.3  ipc bluetooth toggle

at 175.8  scene network
at 176.1  ipc network toggle
at 176.2  caption 4.8 Network: wired with its last speed test, and Wi-Fi in reach
at 181    keys s
at 181.6  caption 12 A speed test from the panel, on Cloudflare or Speedtest.net
at 183    keys 1
# The result goes back to the list by itself 1.5 s after the run ends (about
# 192 s here); no Esc: on the list it would close the panel, and the toggle
# below open it again.
at 194.4  caption 3.2 The result is kept with the connection
at 197    ipc network toggle

at 198    scene tray
at 198.4  caption 7.4 Tray icons keep their own menus
at 198.7  click 1034 22 right
at 204.7  keys Escape

at 206.2  scene polkit
at 206.5  fixture polkit demo-ask
at 206.6  caption 7.7 top Requests for administrator rights are asked by the shell itself
at 212.7  ipc polkit cancel
at 213.2  fixture polkit demo-idle

at 214.7  scene keybindings
at 215    ipc cheatsheet toggle
at 215.1  caption 7.2 top Every key binding, grouped, read from Hyprland
at 221.2  ipc cheatsheet toggle

at 222.7  scene session
at 223    ipc session toggle
at 223.1  caption 5.7 top Lock, log out, reboot, shut down
at 227.7  ipc session toggle

at 229.2  scene lock
at 229.5  lock
at 229.6  caption 4.25 The lock screen
at 234.05 caption 4.25 Every figure in this video is invented data

at 238.7  stop
